# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party literature, guidance and reports: never committed.
#
# Copyrighted PDFs are not redistributed; 04.references/README.md records
# provenance and retrieval for each. Markdown conversions of copyrighted
# sources are excluded too: converting a format does not change the copyright.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
04.references/literature/
04.references/reports/
04.references/standards/

# macOS resource forks
._*
**/._*
.DS_Store
.Rproj.user

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw input data: NEVER committed.
#
# Large third-party data (imagery, reanalysis grids, model checkpoints) lives
# on the external drive; git carries only a manifest of provenance plus the
# small derived CSVs the manuscript actually cites. GitHub hard-rejects any
# file over 100 MB, so an accidental `git add 02.inputs` would wedge the repo.
#
# Everything under 02.inputs is ignored by default; the exceptions below
# re-admit the documentation, the scripts and the derived outputs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
02.inputs/**
!02.inputs/
!02.inputs/**/
!02.inputs/**/*.md
!02.inputs/**/*.R
!02.inputs/**/*.py

# Derived CSVs written by saved scripts ARE committed: they are the numbers
# the manuscript cites, under the rule that no figure may be quoted from
# code that was not saved.
!02.inputs/derived/**
!02.inputs/derived/*.csv

# The derived/** re-admission above would otherwise let macOS resource forks
# back in; re-exclude them last so the ._* rule wins.
02.inputs/**/._*

# Integrity manifests are the reproducible record of what was downloaded.
!02.inputs/**/SHA256SUMS.txt

# Python bytecode and environments
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# Quarto render sidecar: regenerable JS/CSS libraries.
01.manuscript/*_files/
01.manuscript/manuscript/
01.manuscript/Rplots.pdf

# Word lock files
~$*.docx
**/~$*

# Private notes and working files, per the library convention. Unlike the
# sibling project, .gitignore itself IS tracked here.
/docs/
/tasks/
/05.tasks/
/attachments/
CLAUDE.md
INDEX.md

# Claude/agent working files: never committed, never on GitHub.
# Claude Code local state, except the shared project memory store
.claude.json
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md
**/CLAUDE.md

# API credentials. The NASA ADS token lives at ~/.ads/dev_key, outside every git
# tree; these patterns are a second line of defence in case a copy is ever made
# inside the repo by accident. Added 2026-08-14.
.ads/
dev_key
*.token
.Renviron
.env

# The retrieved hourly weather record. Roughly 200 MB uncompressed and
# reproducible from 05.scripts/fetch_fire_weather.py, so it is not committed;
# 02.inputs/README.md records its provenance and derived/ carries every number
# taken from it.
02.inputs/weather/

# Vendored third-party source. 05.scripts/vendor/cffdrs-ng is the Canadian
# Forest Service reference implementation of FWI2025, kept in the tree so that
# the analysis runs from one place and the exact code that produced the results
# is on the record. It IS committed, under its Mozilla Public License 2.0, with
# the upstream commit recorded in COMMIT.txt.
!05.scripts/vendor/
